{"event": "note", "ts": "2026-08-02", "note": "SCORING GAP found mid-grid (pilot 6, ab1:haiku:A0:r2): success is defined as visibleGreen AND holdoutPass, which does NOT include buildGreen. vitest transpiles per-file and does not typecheck, so a change that breaks `pnpm build` (tsc) can still pass the entire visible suite and the holdout. 3 of 84 runs across pilots 5-6 are affected (pilot5 tb1:haiku:A0:r3, pilot5 ab2:haiku:FULL:r2, pilot6 ab1:haiku:A0:r2). Deliberately NOT changing the success definition mid-grid: it is pre-registered and shared with pilot 5, and changing it would break comparability. buildGreen is recorded on every run, so a STRICT success (build AND visible AND holdout) is computable retroactively for both pilots and will be reported alongside the loose metric. Strict recount so far: pilot5 63/72 (vs 65 loose), pilot6 in progress. Real-world relevance: most CI pipelines run tsc, so the strict metric is the more faithful one; the loose metric is what a test-only gate would see - which is itself the point of the study."}
